    <h2 class="section-title">Why Construction Contractors Face Tax Problems</h2>
    <div class="service-content-full">
      <p>Construction contractors deal with large lump-sum payments, expensive equipment, and seasonal work. A big project payment can trigger a huge tax bill, while material costs and equipment maintenance drain cash reserves. Add subcontractor payments and the complexity of job costing, and taxes often get pushed aside.</p>
      <p>The good news? An IRS Installment Agreement lets you pay your tax debt in monthly payments over time. It's the most common way to resolve tax debt, and it's much easier to qualify for than an Offer in Compromise.</p>
    </div>
